Subject: SUMMARY:Increasing swap area?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078701111800

Thanks to those who replied

I resolve the problem after the installation
We make a disk storage with 2 inside disks, one tape, one cdrom and 4
disks externals.So a put one swap area in each disk.

1 - I write the label, using the disklabel
2 - Put the UFS
3 - Put the entry in the fstab
4 - And issue the swapon command.

Now i am working with 5 swap areas.

Works fine!!

Thanks Andre

