     Hi,
     
     The solution to this and probably all the other problems i have had 
     with the console was so simple that I just couldn't see it.
     
     I went into the ECU and investigated the state of the on-board 
     graphics driver. It was disabled. But I tried to SAVE AND QUIT not 
     just quit. And that did the trick.
     
     After that, the command sizer -gr answered only: "1280 x 1024" as it 
     should instead of "640x480 1280x1024".
     
     So, my idea is that the onboard graphics adaptor has been on, and seen 
     as FIRST screen and the "real" one, the PowerStorm has been seen as 
     the SECOND screen. And that is why (according to Tom Blinn) the screen 
     goes black because xlogin makes the second screen go black.  This may 
     also be the explanation of why ,during installation, only the X canvas 
     is visible and the cursor disappears. It simply goes into the first 
     display where everything happens. (by moving the mouse to the right, I 
     could get the cursor visible and the button menus worked correctly).
     
     
     I just talked on the phone with a Digital guy. He told me that the ECU 
     shows the values it would like to save, not the present values.
     
     Thanks again Tom Blinn, David Warren, Don.
     
     Yours, Lars Bro (lbro@dscc.dk)
     
     
     
     
     

