ORIGINAL POSTING
----------------
The list archive web site is not responding right now so forgive me
if this question has already been answered.

I'm in the process of upgrading an Alpha 2100A 5/300 from DU4.0B to
DU4.0D and decided to upgrade the firmware from V4.5-65 to V5.0.
The firmware update notes state that a DU patch is required for the
KZPSA A11 firmware that is part of the V5.0 firmware upgrade.  I went
to the digital patch site but could not find anything listed for 4.0D.

Does anyone know if the required KZPSA patches have been incorporated
into 4.0D?  And if so do I need to wait until after the DU4.0D upgrade
to upgrade the firmware?  And if I do need to wait until after the
OS upgrade will my current firmware (V4.5-65) work with 4.0D?  The
4.0B Installation Guide shows my hardware needing V4.7 of the firmware
even though it has been running fine for many months.  Am I missing
something here?

SUMMARY
-------
Thanks to the following:
	Alan <alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com>
	John F. Marten <root@tigger.oslc.org>
	Alan Davis <Alan.Davis@digital.com>
	John P.Speno" <speno@isc.upenn.edu>
	Martin Mokrejs <mmokrejs@mail.natur.cuni.cz>
	Norm Thomas <normt@ix.netcom.com>

The replies are included below but the consensus was that the KZPSA patches
are included in the 4.0D release.  Nobody addressed the firmware question
so I took a chance and installed 4.0D with my current V4.5-65 firmware.
Immediately after the OS upgrade I upgraded the firmware to V5.0.  This
seemed to work OK except for loosing access to the second CPU.  I was
able to get the second CPU back by using the "clear_errors all" and
"set cpu_enabled ff" commands at the SRM console and power cycling the system.

John Speno sent a list of "DIGITAL UNIX Version 4.0D Fixes" which
was fairly long so I didn't include it here.  If anyone would like
it I would be happy to forward it to you.

Martin Mokrejs suggested not even doing the upgrade until a Jumbo
patch for 4.0D is out.

John Marten provided the URL of the list archives search page.
	http://www-archive.ornl.gov:8000
The URL I had been trying was the higher level "Mailing List Archives"
which has a link to the search page.
	http://www.ornl.gov/its/archives/mailing-lists/
Both are working now so I don't know if I could have reached the search
page while the other page was unreachable.

