From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Mar 19 03:52:11 1998
From: Gil Renard <gilrenard () yahoo ! com>
Date: Thu, 19 Mar 1998 03:52:11 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Passwords in C2
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078701111550

First, I want to thank the following people for their answers:
	
	Jorge Granjal, Richard Young, John Pritchard, Natalia Salzberg,
Michael James, Martin Mokrejs, Don Newcomer, Vialette and Lou Mullikin

My question was: how to make a backup of the all the passwords when
using C2 enhaced security.

Here's my summary:

- There's usefull info ina the authck, convuser and edauth man pages

- Passwords in C2 are kept under /tcb/files/auth in alphabetical order
(DU 3.2)

- Passwords are kept in a database called auth.db under /tcb/files and
under /var/tcb/files

- An option is to take the system out of enhanced security, and then
make a backup copy of /etc/passwd (which will have encrypted passwords)

					Gil Renard
