Hi,

I got back excellent responses.  Thanks to:
Stan Horwitz
Bill CArlson
Christian Miranda
John Becker
Mandell Degerness
Jeff Beck
and Alan @nabeth.cxo.dec.com.

Basically everyone said doing the file command on /dev/rrz*c would give
the answer.
After a few e-mails back and forth with Alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com, I got
the full details
I really needed to get the answer.

Here are the steps I took....

1) file /dev/rrzb43c, that showed me...

     scsi #5 and scsi id #3, which is Bus 5 and Target 3.  Lun 1 is from
the "b" in rrzb43c

2) scu show edt

   look for a device not present on bus 5.

3) hszterm -b 5 -t 3 -l 3  (which is not present on my system. Anything
from bus 5 is ok that
                                     is not present)

4) from the HSZ prompt:  
   show units
   My system comes up with D101, D201 and D301.
   
   I know it is D301 because the 1 is the Lun number which is b in
rrzb43.
   The 3 is the scsi id number taken from the file command on
/dev/rrzb43c
   I know I'm on the right bus also since I did a hszterm -b 5 which I
got from
   the file command which is the scsi number.

D301 uses R1

5) show R1 will shows me disk200, disk210, disk220 and disk230. .

so rzb43c is disk200 disk210 disk220 and disk230 on my system.

another example would be rzb51c which is on bus 6 and is also lun 1
and scsi id 3.  This is also D301 but points to a stripeset using
different
disks.

thanks all!
Allan

