To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: can TZ877 DLT tape drive support DLT compactTape III
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078701111488


Hi,
	Sorry for the long delayed summary. Thanks to:

	Selden E. Ball, Jr.		SEB@LNS62.LNS.CORNELL.EDU
	Mitch Bertone			mbertone@gtech.com
	Dr. Thomas P. Blinn		tpb@zk3.dec.com
	Alan Rollow			alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com
	George Guethlein		GGuethlein@GiantOfMaryland.com

The answer is:
	TZ877 autoloader incorporates a TZ87/TZ87N drive (equivalent to DLT2000)
which does not support DLT compactTape IIITX nor the DLT compactTape IV tape.
They will work with a DLT 4000/7000 tape drive. We have to upgrade the TZ877
to TZ887/TZ897. On the other hand, I found that our Sun is using a DLT4000
and both tapes works.


