From tru64-unix-managers  Mon Mar 09 19:03:19 1998
From: Paul Kitwin <PAUKIT () HBSI ! COM>
Date: Mon, 09 Mar 1998 19:03:19 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY, part 1: How to kill an Alpha Server
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078701111338

CNTL/P is the key combo that drops the server.  What it does is halt CPU
0, and returns to console mode.

This works on 2100/2000s, 8200/8400s, and I believe (though not tested)
4000/4100s.

To bypass/override this:

1) 8200/8400, turn the system key to secure, this disables the console.

2) There should be an SRM variable to disable this.  I have a call
logged w/ DEC to get an answer.

