     The system's disk encapsulation procedure relies on the presence of a
     swap area on the system disk. The best thing to do in your case would
     be to move the usr and var areas on the "other" disk and leave root
     and swap on the boot disk (it does not really matter: root is small
     and not very often used, so separating usr\var from root\swap would
     achive the performance you look for in the same way as if swap was
     apart from root\usr).
     Then, volencap will make it through !


