     and btw, do not reinstall !

     - prepare for lazy mode (remove /sbin/swapdefault and the swap entry
     in /etc/fstab if any)
     - halt system (shutdown -h now)
     - boot sigle user (>>>boot -fl "s")
     - mount /usr (and /var if separate)
     - use the other disk (where swap used to be) to move the usr area over
     there (it is simpler if AdvFS is used with utilities licence: just do
     "addvol" foloowed by "rmvol")
     - repartition the boot disk to get "b" for the swap (use disklabel)
     - rebuild /sbin/swapdefault
         ln -s /dev/rz0b /sbin/swapdefault
        (and reinsert new swap info in fstab)

     I'm sorry for details if too many, I suppose you know all this, but I
     put them here just in case ...


